        "falseColor": true,
        "notes": "Galileo false color: 756 nm → red, 559 nm → green, 404 nm → blue, at 1.4–1.6 km per pixel. Color covers part of the surface. A correction for each observation reduces broad photographed shading; oblique views retain observed monochrome. Overall brightness is matched to the monochrome base, preserving linear band ratios. This is not a human-visible color reconstruction. Photographed shadows and seams can remain; added globe lighting is approximate. Gray grid marks gaps in both sources.",
        "noData": true
